  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of NNN elements. For any ordered triplet (i,j,k)(i, j, k)(i,j,k) such that iii, jjj, and kkk are pairwise distinct and 1≤i,j,k≤N1 \\le i, j, k \\le N1≤i,j,k≤N, the value of this triplet is (Ai−Aj)⋅Ak(A_i-A_j)\\cdot A_k(Ai​−Aj​)⋅Ak​. You need to find the **maximum** value among all possible ordered triplets.\n\n**Note:** Two ordered triplets (a,b,c)(a, b, c)(a,b,c) and (d,e,f)(d, e, f)(d,e,f) are only equal when a=da = da=d **and** b=eb = eb=e **and** c=fc = fc=f. As an example, (1,2,3)(1, 2, 3)(1,2,3) and (2,3,1)(2, 3, 1)(2,3,1) are two different ordered triplets.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of the input contains a single integer TTT - the number of test cases. The test cases then follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum value among all different ordered triplets.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "3≤N≤3⋅1053 \\le N \\le 3 \\cdot 10^53≤N≤3⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1061 \\le A_i \\le 10^61≤Ai​≤106",
      "Sum of NNN over all testcases won't exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105.",
      "Subtasks",
      "**Subtask 111 (30 points)**: Sum of NNN over all cases won't exceed 200020002000.",
      "**Subtask 222 (70 points)**: Original constraint"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3\n1 1 3\n5\n3 4 4 1 2\n5\n23 17 21 18 19",
        "output": "2\n12\n126",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The desired triplet is (3,2,1)(3, 2, 1)(3,2,1), which yields the value of (A3−A2)⋅A1=(3−1)⋅1=2(A_3 - A_2) \\cdot A_1 = (3 - 1) \\cdot 1 = 2(A3​−A2​)⋅A1​=(3−1)⋅1=2.\nTest case 222: The desired triplet is (2,4,3)(2, 4, 3)(2,4,3), which yields the value of (A2−A4)⋅A3=(4−1)⋅4=12(A_2 - A_4) \\cdot A_3 = (4 - 1) \\cdot 4 = 12(A2​−A4​)⋅A3​=(4−1)⋅4=12.\nTest case 333: The desired triplet is (1,2,3)(1, 2, 3)(1,2,3), which yields the value of (A1−A2)⋅A3=(23−17)⋅21=126(A_1 - A_2) \\cdot A_3 = (23 - 17) \\cdot 21 = 126(A1​−A2​)⋅A3​=(23−17)⋅21=126."
      }
    ]
  },
